stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Current: root issued under the current actor epoch
    Current --> Current: Code / Refresh / reissue / receipt with locked active actor
    Current --> CutOff: identity stop commits a higher actor epoch and Zenith event
    CutOff --> CutOff: stale caller / delayed receipt / old root is refused
    CutOff --> [*]: retain historical root and invalidation facts
    note right of Current
        Derived relation between root and canonical actor epochs.
        Actor writer lock precedes OP device, root and grant locks.
        Recheck lifecycle and epoch after acquiring locks.
        Base self-RP claim updates obey the same order.
        Rotation separately rechecks the actor through OP commit.
        No actor or OP lock spans outbound HTTPS.
    end note
    note right of CutOff
        OP invalidation is a separately committed idempotent delivery.
        A recovered actor requires new authority under the current epoch.
        Recovery does not reactivate this historical root.
    end note
